rs before the final block. Select fewer layers for a cheaper or targeted instrument; token-vector creation needs full coverage. Layer numbers start at zero.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"maxSeqLen\",\n          \"label\": \"Maximum tokens per passage\",\n          \"kind\": \"integer\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"default\": \"128\",\n          \"help\": \"Longer text is truncated to this many tokens. Raw text uses the tokenizer’s native special tokens; no chat template is added.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"skipFirst\",\n          \"label\": \"Leading token positions to omit\",\n          \"kind\": \"integer\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"default\": \"16\",\n          \"help\": \"The reference estimator omits early positions and the final token. A passage must have more than this value plus one token after tokenization.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"dimBatch\",\n          \"label\": \"Jacobian dimensions per backward pass\",\n          \"kind\": \"integer\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"default\": \"1\",\n          \"help\": \"A memory/performance control. The model repeats the passage this many times per pass. Larger values need more activation memory; start with 1 on a large model. For example, width 5,376 needs 5,376 backward passes per row at batch 1, or 672 at batch 8. Batching uses more activation memory; it does not promise proportional acceleration.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"checkpointEvery\",\n          \"label\": \"Checkpoint every N considered rows\",\n          \"kind\": \"integer\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"default\": \"4\",\n          \"help\": \"A checkpoint may contain several gigabytes. Smaller intervals preserve more progress but increase disk traffic. Active scratch keeps the latest complete snapshot; completed runs retain their final snapshot.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"dtype\",\n          